A/B: pick eMMC rootdisk by `active_slot` env var (mt7987: R4-Lite).

mtk_ft_system_setup() (from 315-mt7987-select-rootdisk) maps the boot medium
to a /chosen/rootdisk-<media> phandle. For eMMC, also honour the
`active_slot` env: a -> rootdisk-emmc-a, b -> rootdisk-emmc-b (both added
to the eMMC DT overlay). Falls back to slot A when unset, so
a non-A/B / unprovisioned env still boots. Exact strcmp (not slot[0]) keeps
this consistent with the env's `ab_setpart` (`test "$active_slot" = b`): a
malformed active_slot then falls back to slot A on BOTH sides instead of
mismatching (kernel from one slot, rootdisk phandle from the other).

The same selection publishes /chosen/bpirouter,booted-slot as an immutable
boot-time fact. Linux OTA code compares it with the mutable environment and
refuses all slot writes when either value is absent or they disagree.

Note mt7987's hook is `mtk_ft_system_setup` (prefixed), vs mt7986/mt7988's
plain `ft_system_setup`; and EMMC is the last switch case (closing `}` follows).
--- a/board/mediatek/mt7987/mt7987_rfb.c
+++ b/board/mediatek/mt7987/mt7987_rfb.c
@@ -68,6 +68,21 @@
 		;;
 	case MT7987_BOOT_EMMC:
 		media = "rootdisk-emmc";
+		{
+			const char *slot = env_get("active_slot");
+			const char *booted_slot = "a";
+
+			if (slot && !strcmp(slot, "b")) {
+				media = "rootdisk-emmc-b";
+				booted_slot = "b";
+			} else {
+				media = "rootdisk-emmc-a";
+			}
+			chosen = fdt_path_offset(blob, "/chosen");
+			if (chosen > 0)
+				fdt_setprop_string(blob, chosen,
+						   "bpirouter,booted-slot", booted_slot);
+		}
 		break
 		;;
 	}
